{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review conventions relating to MPs\u2019 dress in the Commons Chamber",
        "additional_details": "The House should review conventions relating to dress. We urge the House to refer the matter to the Procedure Committee or pass a resolution permitting attire worn by candidates in election campaigns in the Chamber if identity can be verified for the oath, voting, and security.",
        "background": "Electoral law allows candidates to stand under a commonly used name. However, Commons rules by convention require business-like attire, with guidance issued and enforced by the Speaker. Consequently, a Member elected in character might not be able to sit in the attire they campaigned in.",
